  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_4 : BorelSpace E] [inst_5 : CompleteSpace E] {U : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal},\n  0 < α →\n    α ≤ β →\n      ContDiff ℝ 2 U →\n        (∀ (x v : E), ↑α * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ≤ ↑β * ‖v‖ ^ 2) →\n          have μ := MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.tilted fun x => -U x;\n          have H := fun x =>\n            ∑ i, ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) ((stdOrthonormalBasis ℝ E) i)) ((stdOrthonormalBasis ℝ E) i);\n          MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧\n            MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => ‖gradient U x‖ ^ 2) μ ∧\n              MeasureTheory.Integrable H μ ∧\n                ∫ (x : E), ‖gradient U x‖ ^ 2 ∂μ = ∫ (x : E), H x ∂μ ∧\n                  ∫ (x : E), ‖gradient U x‖ ^ 2 ∂μ ≤ ↑β * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E)",
    "statement_sha256": "fb0e1631711a05ef96df649ad8845a0190d18f39038f229a0d8aab017514afaa",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal denotes nonnegative real numbers; upward arrows are displayed type coercions. Module.finrank is finite real vector-space dimension.",
      "ContDiff R 2 means twice continuously differentiable. fderiv R is the actual Frechet derivative; applying its derivative twice to v evaluates the genuine Hessian diagonal. gradient is the actual real inner-product gradient.",
      "MeasureSpace.volume is canonical Lebesgue volume on the displayed finite-dimensional inner-product space. mu.tilted f is the normalized exponential tilt of mu by f, using Mathlib measure conventions. The assertion IsProbabilityMeasure remains an explicit conclusion.",
      "stdOrthonormalBasis is the canonical orthonormal basis indexed by Fin(finrank). The displayed finite sum uses this full index set, including an empty index set in dimension zero.",
      "Integrable means actual Bochner integrability for the specified measure; the displayed real integrals are Bochner integrals. BorelSpace identifies the measurable structure with the topology.",
      "The full compiled theorem type has been expanded and checked with Meta.isDefEq. Displayed let bindings retain their exact scopes. No source identity or extra theorem conclusion is supplied.",
      "Exact generic Mathlib definition: Measure.tilted nu f := nu.withDensity (fun x => ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (f x) / integral (fun x => Real.exp (f x)) nu)). withDensity multiplies the base measure by the displayed nonnegative extended-real density. ENNReal.ofReal maps a nonnegative real to that value and a negative real to zero. The denominator is a real Bochner integral, whose value is defined as zero when the function is not integrable; real division by zero is zero. This defines the operation in degenerate cases too, without asserting that any such case occurs for the displayed theorem inputs."
    ]
  },
